# Feature Test Coverage Rule

Every feature in the codebase must be covered by automated tests.

**Guidelines:**
- All new features must include appropriate unit, integration, and/or end-to-end tests.
- Existing features should be retroactively covered with tests if not already present.
- Tests must verify both expected behavior and edge cases.
- Pull requests for new features or changes will only be accepted if sufficient test coverage is provided.

**Purpose:**
- Ensures code reliability and prevents regressions.
- Facilitates safe refactoring and future development.
- Increases confidence in the stability of the codebase.

> **Note:** Features without tests are not considered complete and should not be merged until adequate test coverage is achieved.
